"answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative with varying details across communications. It was introduced as a data analytics and cloud storage optimization project with an initial budget of $500,000 (later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, and subsequently approved for $2M by the executive board). Key personnel include Sarah Tan (Analytics), Marcus Cole (Project Leader), Omar Jensen (Lead Developer), and Tom (sharing initial findings). The project involves AI algorithms, IoT, and Web3 technologies, aiming for a 20% efficiency increase. Phases include design, development, and marketing, with kick-offs scheduled between June and July 2023. Security protocols were updated for multi-factor authentication and encryption. Feedback on the prototype was sought by November, and a meeting to discuss budget allocations was set for August 1st."
